# Memory Allocation & Disposal

Session-lifetime native memory uses two cooperating types in `Game.Allocators` and `Game.Collections`.

## SessionRewindableAllocator

Use `SessionRewindableAllocator` for memory blocks and structures that live for the entire session:

- Raw buffers via `AllocateArray<T>()`
- `NativeArray` / `NativeList` created with the allocator handle
- Pool backing blocks (`Pool<T>`, `SegmentsChain.Pool`, …)
- Session-scoped structs such as `EventsStream`, `RollingGrid`

Individual blocks allocated through the rewindable allocator are **not** disposed manually — the allocator frees them in bulk at session teardown.

## DisposeList

Use `DisposeList` to release memory and native containers that require explicit disposal:

- Register every `IDisposable` resource with `disposeList.Add(...)` during construction
- Include the `SessionRewindableAllocator` itself in the list so it is disposed with everything else
- Pass the same session `DisposeList` into subsystem constructors (`Storage`, `EventsStream`, `Pool<T>`, …)

At session end, dispose the list once; it disposes all registered resources in registration order.

## Main-Thread Construction

Most session structures are built on the main thread during startup. That is what makes `DisposeList` viable — it is a managed type and must only be touched from main-thread construction and teardown code.

Job threads (see `threading-jobs` rule) read and write **pre-allocated** buffers; they do not allocate through `SessionRewindableAllocator` or register with `DisposeList`.

## Pattern

```csharp
// ✅ Session setup (main thread)
using var sessionDisposeList = new DisposeList();
var allocator = new SessionRewindableAllocator(initialBlockSize: 64 * 1024);
sessionDisposeList.Add(allocator);

var freeBlocks = new NativeQueue<Pointer<EventsBlock>>(Allocator.Persistent);
sessionDisposeList.Add(freeBlocks);

var storage = new Storage(fileManager, allocator, sessionDisposeList, playerCache);
var eventsStream = new EventsStream(sessionDisposeList, allocator, writerCount, processors);

// Pool: rewindable blocks + explicit queue disposal
var pool = new Pool<MyStruct>(sessionDisposeList, allocator);

// ❌ Per-block disposal for session-lifetime rewindable memory
allocator.AllocateArray<int>(100); // no matching Dispose call needed

// ❌ Native container without registering on DisposeList
var map = new NativeHashMap<int, int>(128, Allocator.Persistent); // leaks unless Added

// ❌ Using DisposeList from a Job
[BurstCompile] struct BadJob : IJob {
    public void Execute() { /* disposeList.Add(...) */ }
}
```
